from pathlib import Path
import json
import pandas as pd
from metric_core import METRICS

def write_reports(out,root):
 out=Path(out);root=Path(root);m=json.loads((out/'analysis_manifest.json').read_text());ref=pd.read_csv(out/'tables/reference_vs_start.csv');cv=pd.read_csv(out/'tables/supervised_nested_CV.csv');added=pd.read_csv(out/'tables/added_information_vs_APL.csv');pca=pd.read_csv(out/'tables/pca_summary.csv');stab=pd.read_csv(out/'tables/ranking_stability.csv');dec=pd.read_csv(out/'tables/decision_table.csv');scale=pd.read_csv(out/'data/scaler_parameters.csv');rd=pd.read_csv(out/'tables/reduced_feature_decisions.csv')
 fam='late_vs_ref__q95__euclidean_reduced';s=stab[stab.score.isin(['contrast__'+fam,'desirability_w0.5__'+fam])];lines=['# Metric-development summary','',f'**Population:** {m["population"]["primary_pairs"]} strict QC-passing tripeptoid pairs. {m["population"]["paired_including_review"]} paired systems including review form a calibration sensitivity set. Two Nfe-Nfnap-Nfe rows remain excluded for unresolved run identity.','', '**Recommendation:** retain the signed physical response vector and separate Effect_B / Effect_M as provisional structural summaries. Do not canonise a scalar biological effect or desirability target from these data. Pair bounded selectivity with magnitude, and apply explicit utilities only after prediction.','', '## Pristine reference and temporal definition','',f'Endpoint-vs-reference versus endpoint-vs-system-start Spearman correlations span {ref.rho.min():.4f}–{ref.rho.max():.4f} across the measured metrics and membranes. See reference_vs_start.csv for metric-specific differences; rank similarity does not establish identical physical values.','', 'Primary persistent-response candidate: existing 80–100 ns morphology medians. Endpoint morphology is a sensitivity comparison. No 80–100 ns APL value is supplied, so APL enters endpoint full-feature candidates but never silently enters an 80–100 ns composite. The 90–100 ns APL mean is retained separately. Single pristine structures do not establish a thermal null distribution.','', '## Does morphology add information beyond APL?','','| Membrane | Feature set | Nested grouped OOF AUROC | Conditional 95% CI | Balanced accuracy |','|---|---|---:|---:|---:|']
 for r in cv.itertuples():lines.append(f'| {r.side} | {r.features} | {r.AUROC:.3f} | {r.auc_ci_low:.3f}–{r.auc_ci_high:.3f} | {r.balanced_accuracy:.3f} |')
 lines+=['','The target is the visual deformation phenotype (curved, bulge_curved or bulge_flat versus plain-flat classes), not antibacterial activity. Inner folds select L2 regularisation; outer folds group molecules. Confidence intervals resample OOF molecule predictions and are conditional on the fitted CV procedure.']
 for r in added.itertuples():lines.append(f'- {r.side}: adding morphology to dAPL changes AUROC by {r.delta_AUROC:+.3f} (paired-bootstrap CI {r.ci_low:+.3f} to {r.ci_high:+.3f}).')
 lines+=['','## PCA and candidate comparison','','| Late-view PCA | PC1 variance | PC1 + PC2 variance | Features |','|---|---:|---:|---:|']
 for side in ['B','M','paired']:
  for scope in ['full','reduced']:
   z=pca[(pca.view=='late_vs_ref')&(pca.side==side)&(pca.feature_set==scope)];lines.append(f'| {side}, {scope} | {z.iloc[0].explained_variance:.1%} | {z.iloc[1].cumulative_variance:.1%} | {z.iloc[0].features} |')
 lines+=['','PCA explains variance, not damage. Absolute PC1 distance retains the pristine origin but can discard physically distinct orthogonal responses. Loadings, explicit sign multipliers and feature contributions are saved.','', 'All three scalings (IQR, no-interaction MAD, q95), full/reduced Euclidean and winsorised shrinkage-Mahalanobis distances, inverse-redundancy weighted sums, absolute PC1, single metrics and directional comparators are evaluated. The main calibration shares scale factors across B/M; membrane-specific scaling is a sensitivity analysis because it can erase real cross-membrane effect differences.','', '**Mathematical findings:** normalised contrast and angular selectivity contain the same rank information: S_angle = (4/π) atan(S_norm). Both need magnitude and have a path-dependent limit at the origin, despite the explicit origin=0 convention. Raw ratios are rejected as stand-alone targets. Stabilised ratios depend on their disclosed pseudocount. Difference collapses both-low/both-high; utilities impose an unvalidated biological trade-off.','', '| Illustrative late q95 reduced ranking | Median bootstrap rank correlation | Mean top-10 overlap |','|---|---:|---:|']
 for r in s.itertuples():lines.append(f'| {r.score.split("__")[0]} | {r.median_rank_rho:.3f} | {r.top10_overlap_mean:.1%} |')
 lines+=['',f'Bootstrap: {m["parameters"]["bootstrap"]} molecule resamples refit calibration and score parameters. These intervals quantify sensitivity to the calibration cohort, **not** thermal trajectory error or uncertainty in pristine reference geometry. Full per-molecule intervals and top-k probabilities are saved for every unsupervised score.','', '## Limits before using these as ML targets','', '- Only four flat_no_interaction systems per membrane. No hard null threshold is validated. Null-MAD is exploratory and its uncertainty is shown.','- No replicated pristine trajectories or raw production trajectories were supplied. Autocorrelation-aware block uncertainty, effective sample size, rare-event kinetics and transition timing remain untested.','- No chemical descriptors or locked train/test manifest were supplied for this task. OOF phenotype alignment is not proof of prediction from peptoid chemistry or extrapolation to new chemical families. No canonical ML model or active-learning selection was changed.','- No microbiological efficacy, cytotoxicity, pore/permeability or independent experimental outcome was supplied. Physical deviation cannot yet be equated to desired bacterial harm or mammalian toxicity.','- Geometry method sensitivity (smoothing/grid/leaflet assignment) is inherited from the supplied workflow; it cannot be re-estimated without alternate reconstructions or frames.','- Target definitions fitted on this analysis cohort are exploratory. Before ML use, derive/freeze parameters on the allowed training/reference set only, keep molecular identities grouped, and evaluate prospectively or with chemical-similarity-aware held-out sets.','', '**Exact next decision:** choose the physical outputs to freeze, rather than declare a winning utility. Proposed shortlist: signed late height, thinning and leaflet-asymmetry responses plus separate B/M summaries; keep APL responses explicitly. Validate repeatability and chemical-model predictability before adopting a scalar.','', 'The analysis code submits no jobs itself. Execution may be inside a scheduler allocation; consult the run log and analysis manifest for the execution context. Source hashes were checked unchanged.']
 (out/'SUMMARY.md').write_text('\n'.join(lines)+'\n')
 dictionary=['# Unified metric data dictionary','','One row per molecule + nmol + physical_run matched B/M pair. `selected_pair` identifies strict QC-passing primary inference; `qc_pass_pair` records both membranes passing the geometry QC. The table retains paired REVIEW rows for sensitivity only.','','- `B` = POPE75POPG25_W_WF; `M` = POPC60CHOL40_W_WF.','- `pristine_reference`: full-precision peptoid-free prod.gro measurement.','- `system_start`: first Pull frame of the individual peptoid-containing simulation.','- `endpoint`: Relax 100 ns.','- `late_80_100_median`: source median over 80–100 ns. APL is deliberately missing here.','- `endpoint_vs_ref`, `late_vs_ref`, `endpoint_vs_start`, `start_vs_ref`: explicitly signed differences.','- `__abs`: absolute value of the preceding signed difference, not a replacement for it.','- `B_minus_M__...`: corresponding B minus M; `abs_B_minus_M__...`: absolute paired difference.','- `*_asym`: |upper−lower| at the time point, then reference subtraction. `*_asym_signed`: upper−lower without taking its absolute value. These answer different questions.','- `ddAPL`: canonical BOX endpoint-minus-system-start APL_B minus the corresponding APL_M.','- `APL__late_90_100_mean`: separate canonical last-10-ns mean; it is never represented as an 80–100 ns statistic.','', '| Metric | Units |','|---|---|']+[f'| {k} | {v[2]} |' for k,v in METRICS.items()]+['','Scores use zero-preserving scaling x/s. No median centring is applied to the pristine deviations before distance calculations. PCA centres internally, while PC1 effect uses the projection of the pristine deviation itself. Effect bounds use d/(1+d), hence [0,1), and can never be interpreted as calibrated biological probabilities.','', 'Missing numeric values are blank CSV fields. Singular raw ratios are explicitly NaN with nonfinite-count tables. Floating-point CSV columns are deterministic and retain 12 significant digits; full model JSON retains native precision.']
 (out/'data/DATA_DICTIONARY.md').write_text('\n'.join(dictionary)+'\n')
 decisions='''# Decisions

- The two peptoid-free prod.gro bilayers are **pristine references**. First Pull frames are **system start**. Existing source field names are mapped explicitly, never relabelled as pristine measurements.
- SASA is excluded. Geometry directly addresses bending, whereas Martini SASA additionally needs a frozen bead-radius/probe convention and evidence of incremental value.
- The strict 156-pair source is authoritative for this snapshot. The Nfe-Nfnap-Nfe legacy-run mismatch is not automatically repaired. REVIEW_REQUIRED systems enter sensitivity only.
- Keep every source metric and signed/absolute deviation. Compare full/reduced spaces using |Spearman rho| ≥ 0.90 and the documented physical retention order; freeze the selected indices and report removals.
- Main late effects use 80–100 ns morphology. Endpoint candidates may include APL. Missing 80–100 ns APL is not filled with its 90–100 ns mean or endpoint.
- Compare shared B/M IQR, no-interaction MAD and q95 scales. Zero stays at the pristine point. Reject degenerate scales explicitly rather than hiding epsilon terms. Null scaling has only eight pooled no-interaction observations and is not a validated noise floor.
- Compare Euclidean, winsorised Ledoit–Wolf covariance distance, inverse-redundancy weighted absolute sums, absolute PC1, single metrics and directional comparators. Shrinkage regularises covariance; it does not establish a biological null. Mahalanobis may downweight common coherent response and is not automatically preferable.
- Bound distance summaries with d/(1+d), a disclosed monotonic display/utility scale. Report all calibration parameters. Do not interpret these as probabilities.
- PCA is exploratory. Largest absolute loading is oriented positive and each multiplier is saved. Absolute PC1 is a comparator, not an endorsed response axis.
- Supervised L2 logistic candidates are phenotype comparators only. They do not have a pristine-zero interpretation and are not combined into the primary selectivity families. Their validation is nested and molecule-grouped.
- Contrast and angle are equivalent directional rankings. Neither identifies response strength. Keep magnitude and B/M effects. Raw ratios are diagnostic-only and rejected as standalone targets.
- Log ratios use c=0.01, 0.1 and 0.5 on the disclosed bounded scale. These are sensitivity values, not noise estimates. No physical noise-floor pseudocount is justified by one pristine frame.
- Geometric, linear and ideal-point utilities use B weights 0.25, 0.5 and 0.75. No preference is hidden. Pareto analysis is the benchmark; magnitude and inverse ratio are not better-is-larger bacterial utilities.
- Classes are nominal validation evidence. Deformed versus plain-flat and bulge-related contrasts are explicitly defined. No single ordinal label mapping is assumed.
- Bootstrap molecules, not membrane rows. Calibration confidence is separate from trajectory uncertainty. Learn every scaler/threshold/feature selection within validation folds.
- No metric is canonised. Until independent physical/biological and predictive validation exists, retain separate per-membrane physical targets and apply utilities after prediction.
'''
 (root/'DECISIONS.md').write_text(decisions)
